WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.897
- The 17-year-old who video recorded

00:00:01.897 --> 00:00:04.680
George Floyd's murder is going to receive

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.140
an honorary Pulitzer Prize,

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:07.660
and I think this is a great development.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.071
So many people felt powerless in the face

00:00:10.071 --> 00:00:13.220
of what was happening to
George Floyd and others,

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.670
and Darnella Frazier,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.870
who was only 17 at the time,

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.630
stood her ground and recorded things.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.180
She was walking home with
her nine-year-old cousin

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.020
when she had the bravery to sit there

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.770
and record everything happening.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.760
Of course, many people
wanted to intervene,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.040
but the fact of the
matter is if you intervene

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.260
in a situation like that,

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.480
you might be charged with
obstruction of justice

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.550
or assaulting a police
officer, and it's not fair,

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.270
but those are the rules.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.960
And what people can do is
when they see something

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.580
that might be suspicious, it's not clear,

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.309
simply record the police
or record the activity.

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:47.680
That's what you can do
as a citizen to prevent

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.790
these kinds of things from
happening in the future.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.170
It's sad but true but the
conviction of Derek Chauvin

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.150
probably wouldn't have happened
without the video evidence,

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:57.070
and we should be encouraging
citizen journalists like this,

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:57.970
as much as we can.

